major function of ferritin is the storage of iron in a soluble and nontoxic state. Defects in ferritin proteins are associated with several neurodegenerative diseases. This gene has multiple pseudogenes. Several alternatively spliced transcript variants have been observed, but their biological validity has not been determined. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P02794","text":"Stores iron in a soluble, non-toxic, readily available form. Important for iron homeostasis. Has ferroxidase activity (PubMed:9003196). Iron is taken up in the ferrous form and deposited as ferric hydroxides after oxidation (PubMed:9003196). Also plays a role in delivery of iron to cells (By similarity). Mediates iron uptake in capsule cells of the developing kidney (By similarity). Delivery to lysosomes is mediated by the cargo receptor NCOA4 for autophagic degradation and release of iron (PubMed:24695223, PubMed:26436293)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[{"accession":"P02794","pdb_id":"4oyn","het_id":"BCN","resolution":1.43,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Green et al. 2024"],"ligand_name":"Bicine","ligand_class":"lipid, detergent, buffer or other additive","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"Fifteen minutes iron loaded human H ferritin","first_author":"Pozzi, C.","n_authors":6,"journal":"Acta Crystallogr.,Sect.D","year":2015,"doi":"10.1107/S1399004715013073","citation_url":"https://doi.org/10.1107/S1399004715013073"},{"accession":"P02794","pdb_id":"4ykh","het_id":"BCN","resolution":1.52,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Green et al. 2024"],"ligand_name":"Bicine","ligand_class":"lipid, detergent, buffer or other additive","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"Thirty minutes iron loaded human H ferritin","first_author"